file tools/fixtures/p/plant_liveness_scan.sh the writing test strips descriptor duplications; --list names the lines behind each count
file tools/fixtures/p/plant_liveness_control.sh six legs, both sides plus the strip removed and the stderr line asserted to count again
file construction/REDS.md %519 accreted with what landed and what stays open; pin trimmed to 40,938 of 40,960
file construction/ITINERARY.md the BAKERY block rewritten to this lap
scope one red worked, two files repaired, two pins accreted
status GREEN on my own work -- plant_liveness witness GREEN, control 74 legs faults=0, both touched files graded B+. The tree carries one red that is not mine (say_compose_bound, 538 of 537) and my cold open read tree_moved=yes by my own hand.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the REDS pin stands at 22 bytes of headroom, so the next row cannot land without your word on the bound; and the ~66 unresolved plants are mostly pen-authored, so whether that population earns a ceiling is a question rather than a sweep.
